  "reference_protocol": "Both public Core file modes compare return code, output/errors and persisted catalog/rows/integrity against pinned SQLite. The twelve raw native-byte cases compare stdout as bytes and assert that reads leave the actual database unchanged. Sixteen additional tests use fresh seeded Unicode data. No oracle answer, mask, skipped failure or output correction is used in execution.",
  "implementation": [
    "After original serial types, payload length and schema/row decoding succeed, an optional IO page-source observer sees the actual physical fields. UTF-16 file and WAL loaders retain only TEXT representations that cannot roundtrip through the logical UTF-8 representation. The cache is keyed by actual table, rowid and column and attached to the opened snapshot.",
    "Typed scalar column lookup attaches native bytes only when the decoded bytes match the current logical value. Every lookup still returns the same logical value/error, proved universally. Scalar hex/octet-length/BLOB casts can then use real source bytes. UTF-8 opens do not install the observer.",
    "Compound result-set keys and ORDER BY specifications receive the actual database encoding. The original source-free component keeps its UTF-8 default and existing state-preservation contract; the encoded variant also has a registered state-preservation theorem.",
    "Window input binding preserves the compiler-owned function head and captured SQL metadata while visiting actual arguments and FILTER predicates. Window partition/order expressions use the actual connection encoding.",
    "Compound alias recognition unwraps value-preserving connection/declaration metadata. Structural matching of value-changing operations remains intact. Its input-annotation alias law is registered.",
    "The exact Runtime.Record/reference IO equality remains unchanged, including callback effects. A new theorem proves that omitting the callback returns exactly the ordinary decoded row."
  ],
  "proof_scope": "Component logical-value preservation, ordinary decode-effect preservation, compound state preservation, exact production/reference record IO equality and transparent alias recognition. No complete encoding translation or global SQLite equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unit and survey share named feature generators. Ten failures remain: triggers, WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys, partial indexes and expression indexes in both file modes. These probes are not a global compatibility percentage.",
